{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-q-expr-sql/mut-field-rule-other-field",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-EXPR-1",
    "EXPR-MUTATION"
  ],
  "description": "EXPR-MUTATION, deciding variant: a field-level rule that names another field, against the same rule at table level. MO(ID, V, R): the V field rule [V] < [R] is set (the put is attributed), (V, R) = (2, 1), (1, 2) and (1, Null) are added; then the field rule is cleared, TableDef.ValidationRule [V] < [R] is set and the same three rows are tried. Follow-up probe (status F) for EXPR-MUTATION; runs on a writable fresh copy of fixture r-q-expr-sql-main through DAO.DBEngine.120; each recordset reads Name, Type and Value of every field. Each statement is preceded by a marker (a DROP TABLE of a table that does not exist, which always fails), so DBEngine.Errors read after the statement shows that statement's own failure or the marker's, never an older one.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
